A||||12||Scott2M4||Just how many different Fieros are there anyway?||||5
Z||000000||Scott2M4||10-11-1999||12:18 PM||||OK, folks.  I'm starting to get into the Fiero rage.  I've saved off many different websites.  I've purchased a few books.  I have a customer ID# from The Fiero Store.  And I'm getting ready to purchase my first (probably) 2M4.<P>My biggest problem right now is trying to grasp just how many different versions of the car existed between 1984 and 1988 and what the differences were between them.<P>Would one of the experts here please provide me with a breakdown of the entire line?  I have a 'Fiero Spotter's Guide' but it only shows differences by year - not by each individual model.<P>Any help is greatly appreciated!  TIA ...||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||10-11-1999||01:20 PM||||Scott, Let me give it a try.......the following will be model years and types, with tranny options (all from memory of course):<P>1984:  all cars are 4 cylinder cars with either a 4 speed manual or a 3 speed automatic.  Models are as follows: 2m4, Indy and SE<BR>1985: 4 speed manual, 5 speed manual (isuzu for 4 cyl cars only) and 3 speed automatic. models are: 2m4, SE and GT.  the GT is the only one with a v-6 2.8 liter engine.<BR>1986 tranny options are the same.  SE develops 85 GT body and 86 GT gets it's on body work, SE also gains a v-6 option and in July (86.5) all v-6 cars get the GETRAG 5 speed option.  <BR>1987: to my knowledge there were no major changes to the cars.  <BR>1988:  only tranny options are Isuzu 5spd (4 cyl cars), 3 speed automatic, and getrag muncie 5spd (all v-6 cars):  Models: 2m4, Formula (v-6 powered coupe), and GT.  All 88's have a upgraded suspension system and are generally considered the cream of the crop (also last year made), T-Tops became a option, in addition to the sunroof.  Most desired car of the bunch...88 GT, 5 speed with T-Tops, if you find one in Yellow real rare!<P>I hope this helps, some things might be off a little   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by bHooper (edited 10-11-1999).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||88 Fiero||10-11-1999||01:40 PM||||The 1988 Fiero as far as the engine where refined a little bit.. The 4 cylinder got a little more HP and the the V6 with some refined as well and also a better fly wheel..||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-11-1999||03:25 PM||||in 86.5 the 4 cyl gets a roller lifter cam set. All other funstions are the same as previous years.<P>in 87 the 4 cyl moves to DIS distributorless ignition, and the 700 series TBI unit. 88 is the same. Listed performance on these motors is 96 HP and around 130FP torque. I didn't think the 4 speed tranny is available anymore in 87. <P>All V6 2.8L motors are functionally identical. there are some changes to the ECM over the years. I think the cold start injector was deleted in later motors.<P>87/88 body work was changed to a diferant nose & tail on the coupes. They finaly did away with the bumper pads. They also use a round trim.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Silver Bullet||10-11-1999||09:56 PM||||bhooper,<P>       Now maybe you can answer my question, according to what you just said, my car would be an 86, although the "vin # cheet sheet" at work says it's an 85.  You said that the 84's didn't have any v6.  then you said that the only v6 in 85 was a GT.  I don't have my title yet, but as far as i knew, my car is an 85 2M6 SE.  Please help me out here.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||10-11-1999||11:53 PM||||From 84-87 there was also a Sport Coupe model, between the base and se. only available with the 4 cyl, I believe||||reg||1
Z||000006||mwbackus||10-12-1999||01:18 AM||||Here is some very good information as to the differences and changes during the years of Fiero production :<BR> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/topfiero/year.txt" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/topfiero/year.txt</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.xnet.com/~paulv/MajorSpecs.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.xnet.com/~paulv/MajorSpecs.htm</A> <P>  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||ChadMan||10-12-1999||08:44 AM||||You're right, SilverBullet:  in 1985, you could get the V6 in the SE, which had the same bodywork as the base coupe.  I always thought these cars were cool because the only external clue to how fast they are is the subtle "2M6" on the deck lid and the extra pair of black (not polished trumpets!) pipes on the passenger side.  Vrrrooom!||||reg||1
Z||000008||bHooper||10-12-1999||10:51 AM||||well one thing I do know about Fiero's......there is alway's something else to learn about them!  i did not know about the '85 "stealth" 2m6 car.||||reg||14
Z||000009||Silver Bullet||10-12-1999||05:15 PM||||The body style of my car does lead alot of people to believe that it's a 4 banger, which in turn, brings me alot of unsuspecting victims!!!! lol||||reg||14
Z||000010||lowCG||10-12-1999||09:10 PM||||My old car was an '86 S/E,4cyl,5sp,with the 4 megaphone exhaust,usually found on 6 cylinder cars,haven't seen many like that.||||reg||1
Z||000011||RFMike||10-13-1999||08:40 PM||||Actually, the 86.5 GT was still available with a 4 speed.  I have one, and yes it is stock.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Carrolles||10-14-1999||06:36 PM||||I have an 85 SE 2m6 4 spd and love it, although it would be nice to have the 5th gear that the Getrag has for highway travel.<P>The basic body styles were<BR>Coupe - 4 cyl all years, notchback body.<P>SC  Sport Coupe - 4 cyl all years, notchback body pointy nose. Black bumper pads for 84 through 85.<P>SE - Special Edition (?) 84 through 87 available with v-6 option starting in 85, notchback body. Pointy nose on 84 and 85 with black bumper pads.  Later years have mild ground effect nose.<P>GT - 85 through 88.  All GTs have v-6.  85 GT and early 86 GT is notchback with aero nose like the Indy.  86 1/2 through 88 are fastback with aero nose and rocker panel ground effects.<P>Formula - 88 only (replaces SE) v-6 only.  Slight Aero nose with notchback.<P>Indy - 84 only with Aero nose and notchback, 4 cyl only.<P>I think this is right (could be wrong on a few details).||||reg||1
